statement:
Let P, n be natural numbers, K ⊆ V ⊆ ℝ^P with K compact and V open, β : ℝ^P → Λⁿ(ℝ^P) continuous on K with |β(x)| ≤ 1 for x ∈ K (|·| = covectorEuclideanNorm), and δ > 0. Then there is an n-form ω : ℝ^P → Λⁿ(ℝ^P) such that:
- ω is C^∞ with compact support (IsTestForm ω);
- tsupport ω ⊆ V;
- |ω(x)| ≤ 1 for all x ∈ ℝ^P;
- |ω(x) − β(x)| ≤ δ for all x ∈ K.
